    <heading level="1">Technology</heading>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, express the equations in slope intercept form (rounding each number to the thousandths place). Enter this into a graphing calculator as Y1, then adjust the ymin and ymax values for your window to include where the y-intercept occurs. State your ymin and ymax values.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="47" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$y - y_{1} = m\left( x - x_{1} \right),$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$y=0.245x-45.662. y=0.245x-45.662.$$ Answers may vary. $$y min =-50, y max =-40 y min =-50, y max =-40$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="48" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$x$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
